# Customer-specific migrations directory (LWM template / WordPress-style refactor)
#
# Purpose: when a client (e.g. clients/laborwasser/api) needs to add custom DB columns
# or tables that are NOT part of the upstream api-base template, they go here.
#
# Usage from a client repo:
#
#   # Run only customer migrations:
#   php artisan migrate --path=database/migrations/customer/
#
#   # Run template + customer migrations together (default behaviour):
#   php artisan migrate
#
# Naming: keep the standard Laravel timestamp prefix and a descriptive suffix:
#   2026_05_06_000001_add_internal_code_to_products.php
#
# Conflicts on upstream merge: if upstream renames or removes a column you depend on,
# resolve in this directory by adding a new migration that re-adds it. Do NOT edit
# upstream migrations.
